helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080202.xhp	0	help	par_id3151041				0	pt	\<emph\>Número:\</emph\> qualquer expressão numérica para a qual queira calcular o logaritmo natural.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080202.xhp	0	help	par_id3150869				0	pt	O logaritmo natural é o logaritmo para a base e. A base e é uma constante com um valor aproximado de 2,718282...				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080202.xhp	0	help	par_id3153968				0	pt	É possível calcular logaritmos para qualquer base (n) e para qualquer número (x) dividindo o logaritmo natural de x pelo logaritmo natural de n, como se segue:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080202.xhp	0	help	par_id3145420				0	pt	Log n(x) = Log(x) / Log(n)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080202.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155131				0	pt	Exemplo:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080202.xhp	0	help	par_id3152463				0	pt	Sub ExemploLogExp				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080202.xhp	0	help	par_id3145750				0	pt	Dim a as Double				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080202.xhp	0	help	par_id3151116				0	pt	Dim const b1=12,345e12				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080202.xhp	0	help	par_id3146985				0	pt	Dim const b2=1,345e34				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080202.xhp	0	help	par_id3148616				0	pt	a=Exp( Log(b1)+Log(b2) )				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080202.xhp	0	help	par_id3149262				0	pt	MsgBox "" & a & chr(13) & (b1*b2) ,0,"Função Multiplicação por logaritmo"				20200411 15:09:53
